INT. MERIDIAN LOGISTICS - WELLNESS NAP POD ROOM - DAY

Six egg-shaped pods. Ambient whale music. A laminated sign reads "SYNERGY RECHARGE: 15 MIN MAX."

GWENDOLYN "GWEN" PRATT, 40s, lanyard, tired eyes, sits on a pod with a laptop. TOBIAS LINDQVIST, 30s, quarter-zip, enters carrying a kombucha.

TOBIAS
Gwen. Didn't know anyone used these.

GWEN
I'm not napping. I'm hiding.

TOBIAS
Same. Can I hide here too?

GWEN
Pod four is warmer.

He sits in pod four. Sips his kombucha.

TOBIAS
Is the all-hands still at three?

GWEN
It moved to four. Then back to three. Then it became a "pre-sync."

TOBIAS
What do we pre-sync?

GWEN
The post-sync.

TOBIAS
Right.

Beat. The whale music swells.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
Gwennie, did you read the memo about the memo?

GWEN
I summarized it. Toby, it said please stop using the word "deliverable."

TOBIAS
I'll circle back on that.

GWEN
That's the word we're not supposed to say.

TOBIAS
Which one?

GWEN
All of them.

He nods. Lies back in the pod. Closes his eyes.

TOBIAS
Wake me at three.

GWEN
It's three.

TOBIAS
Wake me at four.
